# counter harness. One force call is one RgpotCounter.calculate entry.
# v2 success is under the cap, at the force stop, and Hessian index 0.
# energy and Kabsch RMSD were not applied: the problem file has no energy_tol, rmsd_tol, or per-start reference.
# energy_min and energy_max are the final potential values on the recorded points.
# LJ38 index removes the six rigid modes. A curvature is negative only below -max(force_norm, 1e-8*||H||_F, 1e-6).
# Default row. The callback evaluates the harness Lennard-Jones potential and stops on the unscaled force norm. LD_LBFGS, LD_VAR2, and LD_SLSQP scale the objective by maxstep divided by the initial force norm, with maxstep 0.2, so the first identity-Hessian step has that length. Luksan tolg is 1e-8 times the scale. LD_TNEWTON_PRECOND_RESTART recenters a coordinate box of half-width 0.2 until the force stop. LD_MMA keeps the library defaults, including the moving-asymptote sigma of 1. The same values are used for every start.
